    <!-- Law Details -->
    <string name="domestic_violence_act_details">The Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act 2005 provides for:\n\n
        • Protection against physical, sexual, verbal, emotional, and economic abuse\n
        • Right to reside in the shared household\n
        • Protection orders against the abuser\n
        • Monetary relief and compensation\n
        • Custody orders for children\n
        • Free legal aid and counseling services</string>

    <string name="dowry_act_details">The Dowry Prohibition Act 1961:\n\n
        • Prohibits giving or taking of dowry\n
        • Punishment: Up to 5 years imprisonment and fine\n
        • Makes demands for dowry punishable\n
        • Provides for appointment of Dowry Prohibition Officers\n
        • Shifts burden of proof to the accused</string>

    <string name="workplace_harassment_act_details">Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace Act 2013:\n\n
        • Defines sexual harassment at workplace\n
        • Mandates Internal Complaints Committee\n
        • Provides for Local Complaints Committee\n
        • Ensures confidentiality\n
        • Protection against victimization\n
        • Time-bound redressal mechanism</string>

    <string name="pocso_act_details">Protection of Children from Sexual Offences Act 2012:\n\n
        • Protects children from sexual abuse\n
        • Establishes Special Courts\n
        • Child-friendly procedures\n
        • Stringent punishment for offenders\n
        • Mandatory reporting of cases\n
        • Speedy trial of offenses</string>

    <string name="maternity_act_details">Maternity Benefit Act 1961:\n\n
        • 26 weeks of paid maternity leave\n
        • Work from home options\n
        • Crèche facility in establishments\n
        • No dismissal during pregnancy\n
        • Leave for miscarriage and medical termination\n
        • Nursing breaks after returning to work</string>

